Make qubes-session tolerate a missing systemd user manager.  Upstream syncs
the session environment with "dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd
--all"; the --systemd flag requires a systemd user manager and fails without
one.  Guard the --systemd variant on systemctl availability and fall back to
the dbus-only sync otherwise.  On systemd distributions the behavior is
unchanged (systemctl is present, so the original command runs); only systemd-
less sessions (e.g. native Guix, which uses the Shepherd) take the fallback.

Upstream: QubesOS/qubes-gui-agent-linux, appvm-scripts/usrbin/qubes-session.
Status: should-upstream (portable: preserves the existing systemd behavior and
only adds a fallback for systemd-less sessions); intended for submission to the
Qubes project.

diff --git a/appvm-scripts/usrbin/qubes-session b/appvm-scripts/usrbin/qubes-session
index 3cbbbcc..6a1d2e0 100755
--- a/appvm-scripts/usrbin/qubes-session
+++ b/appvm-scripts/usrbin/qubes-session
@@ -53,7 +53,11 @@ UPDTYPE=$(/usr/bin/qubesdb-read /qubes-vm-updateable)
 
 # Sync environment variables from the user session into the systemd user
 # manager and dbus-daemon
-dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd --all
+if command -v systemctl >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd --all
+else
+    dbus-update-activation-environment --all
+fi
 
 # process /etc/xdg/autostart and friends (according to Desktop Application
 # Autostart Specification)
